      "explanation": "<p>Among the given species only K<sub>2</sub>CrO<sub>4</sub> is diamagnetic as central metal atom Cr in it has [Ar]3d<sup>0</sup> electronic configuration i.e., all paired electrons. The structure and oxidation state of central metal atom of this compound are as follows</p>\n<p>Structure</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 24 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kywgtxcv/55ff3871-6aca-45f2-bd13-ad6ba69828f7/16480200-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgtxcx.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n<p>Oxidation state Cr<sup>6+</sup></p>\n<p>Rest all the compounds are paramagnetic. Reasons for their paramagnetism are given below.</p>\n<p>(i) H-atom have 1s<sup>1</sup> electronic configuration i.e., 1 unpaired electron.</p>\n<p>(ii) NO<sub>2</sub> i.e. </p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 24 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kywgwnho/1a89b5fc-8f2c-4eff-8d27-9e184041f5ce/621622c0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywgwnhp.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n<p>in itself is an odd electron species.</p>\n<p>(iii) O<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.673ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.432ex\" height=\"2.537ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 633.1 1121.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-297.3) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (Superoxide) has one unpaired electron in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>* molecular orbital.</p>\n<p>(iv) S<sub>2</sub> in vapour phase has O<sub>2</sub> like electronic configuration i.e., have 2 unpaired electrons in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>* molecular orbitals.</p>\n<p>(v) Mn<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> has following structure</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 24 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kywh07ph/c380f8d6-5457-4f1e-b587-7f77b6237def/c5218350-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh07pi.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n<p>Thus, Mn is showing +2 and +4 oxidation states. The outermost electronic configuration of elemental Mn is 3d<sup>5</sup>4s<sup>2</sup>. Hence, in both the above oxidation states it has unpaired electron as</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 24 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kywh1sbg/f8395e55-5323-43ae-a156-8a8c25e8b8c6/f0dc6dc0-7f28-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh1sbh.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n(vi) (NH<sub>4</sub>)<sub>2</sub>FeCl<sub>4</sub> has Fe as central metal atom with +2 oxidation state. The electronic configuration of Fe<sup>2+</sup> in the complex is<p></p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 24 English Explanation 5\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kywh33dg/5859a8d7-4ad9-4d06-802d-3230af1c5fe5/1535d940-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh33dh.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n<p>(vii) (NH<sub>4</sub>)<sub>2</sub>NiCl<sub>4</sub> has Ni as central metal atom with +2 oxidation state. The electronic configuration of Ni<sup>2+</sup> in the complex is</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywh4fpg/844f63b9-7359-421c-8155-93739a36c220/3a8bf440-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh4fph.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywh4fpg/844f63b9-7359-421c-8155-93739a36c220/3a8bf440-7f29-11ec-a207-df8a0438c2ad/file-1kywh4fph.png\" loading=\"lazy\